{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Abd Manaf, Forefather of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)",
  "data": "At the grave of Abd Manaf in Jannat al-Mu'alla, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا السَّيِّدُ النَّبِيْلُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SAYYIDUN NABEEL\nPeace be upon you, O noble master.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الْغُصْنُ الْمُثْمِرُ مِنْ شَجَرَةِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ الْخَلِيْلِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAL GHUSNUL MUTHMIRU MIN SHAJARATI IBRAAHEEMAL KHALEEL\nPeace be upon you, O fruitful branch of the tree of Ibrahim, the Friend (of Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا جَدَّ خَيْرِ الْوَرٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA JADDA KHAYRIL WARAA\nPeace be upon you, O forefather of the best of creation.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ الْاَصْفِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNAL ANBIYAA'IL ASFIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O son of the chosen prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَابْنَ الْاَوْصِيَاۤءِ الْاَوْلِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAABNAL AWSIYAA'IL AWLIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O son of the successors, the friends (of Allah).\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدَ الْحَرَمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAYYIDAL HARAM\nPeace be upon you, O master of the Sanctuary.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ مَقَامِ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHA MAQAAMI IBRAAHEEM\nPeace be upon you, O heir of the Station of Ibrahim.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَاحِبَ بَيْتِ اللّٰهِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAAHIBA BAYTILLAAHIL A'ZEEM\nPeace be upon you, O custodian of the House of Allah, the Almighty.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰى اٰبَاۤئِكَ وَاَبْنَاۤئِكَ الطَّاهِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAA AABAA'IKA WA ABNAA'IKAT TAAHIREEN\nPeace be upon you and upon your pure forefathers and descendants,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "Abd Manaf, son of Qusayy, is the forefather of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.): the father of Hashim, the father of Abdul Muttalib. Like his father before him, he was a chief of Makkah and of the Ka'bah, and he is buried in al-Hajun, the cemetery of Makkah now called Jannat al-Mu'alla.\n\nThis ziyarat is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj among the ziyarats of al-Hajun, as in Sayyid Muhammad Rida al-Golpayegani's Manasik al-Hajj."
}
